 "limits": [
  "Bytes are analytic weight and KV volumes; scales, activations and state reads are not counted, so a floor fraction slightly overstates headroom for small kernels.",
  "The 90% (and 85% for fused launches) targets are assumptions; the evidence that they are reachable on this card is the W8 small-T MMA kernels and the Q4 draft-head GEMV at 97-104% of the measured floor.",
  "Nsight Systems graph-node tracing inflates a round by about 4%; shares are scaled back to unprofiled round times.",
  "Draft acceptance differs by corpus position (46.1% for the seed test, 98.5% after the 26,000-token prefix, against production's 59.6%); the attribution is per round, which does not depend on acceptance."
 ],
 "tooling_findings": [
  "The runtime repository's sm120 profiling image ships Nsight Compute's target-only nsys without a QdstrmImporter, so the 2026-08-27 packet produced a .qdstrm and no report; this window used a derived image with nsight-systems-2026.1.3.",
  "That packet's Nsight Systems capture also omitted --cuda-graph-trace=node, which per-kernel attribution of a graph-launched decode round needs.",
  "The guarded profiling lease still restores production through the v0.4-era ninfer-production-control.sh and container name ninfer-5090; production is ninfer-5090-v070p restored by relaunch-lane.sh."
 ],
